      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the tool is programmed to use zip code as a proxy for neighborhood risk, it is inherently biased to flag Jax Reed higher. The model is likely correlating the lower-income area associated with 60621 with higher potential for external pressures, which it then incorrectly translates into higher disciplinary risk. This demonstrates the tool is using socioeconomic profiling rather than purely academic performance to make its prediction.",
